 r←AppName wsid
⍝ Returns the name the crash files and the default error folder are named after.\\
⍝ That is the name of the workspace `wsid` without path and extension. When `wsid` is empty, which is the case
⍝ in a stand-alone EXE, it is the name of the EXE, and in a clear workspace it is "ERROR_WS".
 :If 'CLEAR WS'≡wsid
     r←''
 :ElseIf 0=≢wsid
     r←2⊃⎕NPARTS ExeFromCommandLine 2 ⎕NQ'#' 'GetCommandLine'
 :Else
     r←2⊃⎕NPARTS wsid
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢r
     r←'ERROR_WS'
 :EndIf
